  "notes": "FILED ON BOTH TRIGGERS (delta -26.5, and band crossing Established to Developing — a two-band movement). RECOMMENDATION IS flag-for-review, NOT downgrade: the baseline is a 22-company seed placeholder and the movement is chiefly a placeholder correction. CONFIDENCE IS MEDIUM — higher than the other four rotation entities, because unlike them IHG carries genuine documented adverse evidence: two recorded non-responses to Business & Human Rights Resource Centre allegations (Gulf migrant-worker exploitation; California strike-replacement with vulnerable migrants including children, prompting an LA County District Attorney investigation), a UN Global Compact complaint from Unite the union over anti-union conduct, and a class action proceeding in federal court. IHG lands at 34.4, below both Marriott International (44.4, de-seeded 08-18) and Hyatt Hotels (44.4, this cycle). That ordering is defensible: Hyatt settled its strike with a unanimous ratification and Marriott has the sector's strongest documented anti-trafficking training programme, while IHG's distinguishing feature is a documented pattern of declining to answer. ENTITY-RECORD OBSERVATION: the published name \"InterContinental Hotel\" appears truncated relative to InterContinental Hotels Group PLC; logged for coordinator review, not silently renamed. RECOMMEND A TARGETED PASS on: the Bloomberg Law class action's substance and status, the LA County DA investigation outcome, and IHG's 2025 and 2026 Responsible Business Reports.",
